: 1.) Old High German hwio, from older hwēo, from Proto-Germanic *hwaiwa; cognate with Gothic 𐍈𐌰𐌹𐍅𐌰 (ƕaiwa). 2.) Old High German hwē, hwie, from Proto-Germanic *hwē; cognate with Gothic 𐍈𐌴 (ƕē). The latter is a variant of Proto-Germanic *hwī, whence English why, and is further a fossilized instrumental case of *hwaz, *hwat (“who, what”). Form 1 is also related to this stem. Outside of High German the only direct modern cognate is Limburgish wie."]],"senses":[[3321,"wie","adv","how",0],[3322,"wie","conj","like",1],[3323,"wie","conj","as",2],[3324,"wie","conj","than",3,null,["colloquial","nonstandard","Austria","Southern-Germany"]],[3325,"wie","conj","when (referring to the past)",4,null,["colloquial","Austria"]]]},"durchwachse":{"inflections":[["durchwachse","durchwachsen","first-person,indicative,present,singular,subordinate-clause"]]},"gnadenstosses":{"inflections":[["gnadenstosses","gnadenstoss","genitive"]]},"paläolithischem":{"inflections":[["paläolithischem","paläolithisch","dative,masculine,singular,strong,without-article"]]},"rudelbumst":{"inflections":[["rudelbumst","rudelbumsen","present,singular,third-person"]]},"unzukömmlicheres":{"inflections":[["unzukömmlicheres","unzukömmlich","comparative,neuter,nominative,singular,strong,without-article"]]},"weiterhülfest":{"inflections":[["weiterhülfest","weiterhelfen","formal,rare,second-person,singular,subjunctive,subjunctive-ii,subordinate-clause"]]}}}